---
title: "record_attendance_by_card (kintai-v3: Attendance Management)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_normalize: cardId = cardId.replace(/:/, '').toLowerCase()
    q_normalize --> q_rpc: supabase.rpc('record_attendance_by_card', p_card_id)
    q_rpc --> q_lookup: SELECT user_id FROM attendance.users WHERE card_id = p_card_id
    q_lookup --> q_not_found: user_id IS NULL
    q_not_found --> [*]: return {success=false, message='unregistered card'}
    q_lookup --> q_get_member: user_id found
    q_get_member --> q_get_display: SELECT display_name, discord_uid FROM member.members
    q_get_display --> q_fallback_name: display_name IS NULL
    q_fallback_name --> q_get_last: SELECT global_name FROM auth.users
    q_get_display --> q_get_last: display_name found
    q_get_last --> q_determine_type: SELECT type FROM attendances ORDER BY timestamp DESC LIMIT 1
    q_determine_type --> q_insert: new_type = (last='in' ? 'out' : 'in')
    q_insert --> q_return_success: INSERT INTO attendances(user_id, card_id, type, timestamp, date)
    q_return_success --> q_nickname_fallback: success AND user.display_name IS NULL AND discord_uid exists
    q_return_success --> [*]: return {success=true, type, user}
    q_nickname_fallback --> q_cache_name: fetchMemberNickname(discord_uid)
    q_cache_name --> [*]: update display_name in DB (async), return result
    q_rpc --> q_error: RPC error or exception
    q_error --> [*]: return {success=false, message='error'}

    note right of q_determine_type
        INV-001: new_type toggles between 'in' and 'out' based on last record
        INV-002: first attendance for a user defaults to 'in' (last_type IS NULL)
        INV-003: SECURITY DEFINER function runs with elevated privileges
        INV-004: card_id is normalized (lowercase, colons removed) before lookup
    end note

    note right of q_insert
        INV-005: date is computed as JST timezone date, not UTC
        INV-006: Single RPC call replaces 3 separate HTTP requests
    end note
